{"id":"chatcmpl-c75bb28b-bedd-4329-a1dc-455ffed37c7f","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229533,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a verification-heavy approach to spatial/medical image interpretation where laterality and orientation markers are critical. The strategy combines independent expert tools, grounded reporting, and targeted region-of-interest zooming to cross-validate a single finding before committing. The key insight is reconciling image-space orientation (markers) with anatomical laterality to avoid left/right errors.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a task involves left/right or spatial laterality, explicitly reconcile image-space orientation markers with anatomical convention before answering.\",\n    \"Use multiple independent evidence sources (expert query, grounded report, visual zoom) to cross-validate a single high-stakes finding rather than relying on one.\",\n    \"Zoom into the specific region of interest to directly compare competing hypotheses (e.g., which side is higher) instead of judging from the full image.\",\n    \"Before finalizing, run an explicit verification step that states the risk (e.g., marker confusion, normal asymmetry) and confirms the finding is genuine.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Always check orientation markers (LT/RT) and reconcile with anatomical laterality; use ROI crops to compare symmetric structures directly.\",\n    \"Spatial/laterality judgments\": \"Identify the orientation convention first, then map observed features to anatomical sides before selecting an answer.\",\n    \"High-stakes single-answer selection\": \"Gather 2-3 independent confirmations and articulate the specific failure risk in a final verification step.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm orientation marker and map image-left/right to patient laterality before answering.\",\n    \"Verify the finding is true abnormality vs. normal asymmetry using a zoomed ROI comparison.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":604,"total_tokens":966,"completion_tokens":362,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":604},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":362}}}